        "content": "As a father who sees himself as the primary protector and provider for his family, much of my focus is on long-term security, financial stability, and being someone my children can rely on. I’m used to making firm decisions, handling pressure quietly, and taking responsibility when things go wrong. Carrying that role over many years has shaped how I evaluate risks and make choices. Do you think long-term roles centered on protection and provision influence someone's overall decision-making style?"
